  "notes": "These figures (34/67/67/989/1979/1979/3958/3958 TFLOPS, 3.35TB/s) are NVIDIA's FINAL specs, current on the live nvidia.com/en-us/data-center/h100/ product page as of 2026-09-06. An earlier archived NVIDIA datasheet PDF (doc 2287922, May 2022) stated lower PRELIMINARY figures (30/60/60/1000/2000/2000/4000/4000 TFLOPS, 3TB/s) that were explicitly footnoted 'Preliminary specifications, may be subject to change' -- confirmed via Wayback Machine snapshots that NVIDIA revised these upward to the final figures used here by October 2022. Do not use the May 2022 preliminary numbers. TF32/BF16/FP16/FP8/INT8 Tensor Core figures are sparse-only per NVIDIA's footnote convention, no independently published dense value. process_node_nm of 4 represents TSMC's custom '4N' process (a marketing-named node, not a strict linear feature-size figure) used for the GH100 die.",
